      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number [ⲕⲉ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. The running title [ⲙⲡⲥⲁϩ] stands in brackets; its stroke (869–882) is over ⲙ only. Measured stroke over ⲙ of ⲙⲡⲁⲣⲑⲉⲛⲟⲥ (923–936).</p>
        <p n="2" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket opened before ⲉⲧⲟⲩⲁⲃⲉ is closed only on l. 3 after ⲧ; it is closed here at the line end and reopened on l. 3.</p>
        <p n="3" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket closed after ⲧ was opened on l. 2; it is reopened here at the line start. The dot under ⲓ of ⲛⲥⲟⲫⲓⲁ is separate from the letter (6× zoom), so ⲓ and ⲁ are both dotted.</p>
        <p n="4" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ϩⲛ (886–905): ϩ 50 %, ⲛ 60 %, encoded on both. An enlarged ⲛ begins ⲛⲉⲓ̈ⲉⲧϥ.</p>
        <p n="6" ana="#tr.print">Three measured strokes: over the first ⲙ (622–636), over ⲙⲛ (650–671; ⲙ 55 %, ⲛ 57 %) and over the first ⲣ of ⲣⲣⲟ (699–710).</p>
        <p n="7" ana="#tr.layout">Chapter opening: the numeral ⲇ (4) centred with an overline (908–943); the title follows in ll. 8–10. The marginal numerals ⲇ̄ (left 648–674, right 1209–1235) stand beside l. 9.</p>
        <p n="10" ana="#tr.reading">The dot under ϩ of ⲁϩⲁⲛ sits left of the descender (6× zoom).</p>
        <p n="11" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="13" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket opened after ⲡϣⲁ is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end. The dot under ⲡ of ⲡⲉ is below the detector's area threshold but clear at 6×.</p>
        <p n="14" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over [ⲙⲛⲧ] (1318–1339): ⲙ 50 %, ⲛ 62 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="20" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="23" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ inside the restoration; the whole line is restored.</p>
        <p n="24" ana="#tr.print">After ⲡⲉⲧϫⲁⲩⲗⲉ a blurred black vertical mark of letter height (x 1174–1182) stands before the six dots; it is not a letter or dot of the edition's sigla and is not encoded.</p>
        <p n="26" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲡⲛⲁ of ⲙⲡⲡ[ⲛ]ⲁ (1177–1249): second ⲡ 100 %, ⲛ 100 %, ⲁ 70 %; not over the first ⲡ (10 %) or ⲙ.</p>
        <p n="30" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲡ begins ⲡⲙⲁϩϥⲧⲁⲩ after the editors' "leer". Measured overline over ⲓⲏⲥ (1200–1241) covers all three letters.</p>
        <p n="31" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over the first ⲣ of ⲡⲡⲣⲓ̈ⲉ (578–590).</p>
        <p n="33" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲛ begins ⲛⲉⲓ̈ after the closing bracket.</p>
        <p n="35" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲛ begins ⲛⲉⲓ̈ⲉⲧϥ inside the restoration.</p>
      </div>
